  "/*\n * Ink — an additional, opt-in dark theme for @preact-components/theme.\n *\n * Option A from #257: a second selector, applied together with `.dark` (this palette is dark-only,\n * so it never runs without it). It repaints the same custom properties `tokens.css`/`preset.css`\n * already read through `var(--token, <default>)`, so every existing preset rule — buttons, cards,\n * forms, tables — picks the ink colours up. `tokens.css`'s `:root`/`.dark` blocks are untouched: a\n * consumer that never applies `data-theme=\"ink\"` renders exactly as before. `preset.css` gained one\n * addition for this: `.btn`'s focus ring now reads `var(--color-focus-ring, currentColor)` instead\n * of the browser's default `currentColor`, because `currentColor` on `.btn-primary` is that\n * button's own text colour — on ink's accent that text colour is near-black, so a ring drawn in it\n * sat near-invisible against the page. No default palette defines `--color-focus-ring`, so that\n * change is a no-op there.\n *\n * Ink also ships a handful of tokens no default rule reads today — the surface scale, hairline and\n * text-tone tokens below. They exist for a consuming site's own bespoke markup (a navigation rail,\n * a bottom tab bar), not for anything in this package, which is why they have no light-mode or\n * default-dark counterpart: nothing here has a use for them outside `ink`.\n *\n * `--color-primary` here is spent on one thing only — the primary action's own background — unlike\n * the default palette's `--color-primary`, whose own doc comment in `tokens.css` names it for\n * \"buttons, links, focus rings, active nav\" all at once. `--color-nav-active` carries a rail's\n * current-item indicator instead (a foreground/indicator colour — the surface a rail paints behind\n * its current item is `--color-surface-active` above, a separate token), and `.btn`'s own focus\n * ring reads `--color-focus-ring` rather than the accent. Both are the same light neutral, not the\n * accent, so neither competes with a page's one primary button for the same colour. What still does\n * carry the accent, unchanged: links (`btn-link`, `.text-primary`, `.border-primary`), an input or\n * select's own focus ring, checkboxes and radios, `btn-primary-outline`, and `.bar` — all of them\n * read `--color-primary`/`--color-primary-muted` directly, in `preset.css`, and this file repaints\n * those two tokens the same way it repaints every other one. That is by design: an accent-coloured\n * link or a focused input is not competing with anything, it is the accent doing the one job\n * `--color-primary` is for everywhere else in this preset — only a rail's *current-item* indicator\n * and a *button's* focus ring were the two cases #257 asked to split off it.\n *\n * Not an importable specifier once installed, for the same reason as `tokens.css`/`preset.css` —\n * see that file's own header. `@preact-components/theme`'s `+index.ts` exports this file's text as\n * `INK_CSS`, generated by `generate.ts` the same way `TOKENS_CSS`/`PRESET_CSS` are; `README.md` →\n * \"Theming\" → \"Ink\" has the splice-in recipe.\n */\n\n.dark[data-theme=\"ink\"] {\n  /* Re-paint the tokens preset.css already reads, so buttons, cards, forms and tables repaint. */\n  --color-surface: oklch(0.26 0.014 260); /* card */\n  --color-canvas: oklch(0.15 0.012 260); /* page */\n\n  --color-border-subtle: oklch(0.34 0.014 260);\n  --color-border-control: oklch(0.4 0.016 260);\n\n  --color-foreground: oklch(0.93 0.006 260); /* primary text tone */\n  /* 0.68, not the surface scale's own 0.66 step: muted text needs to clear 4.5:1 against every\n     surface it can sit on, including --color-surface-active (0.3), and 0.66 only cleared 4.41:1\n     there. */\n  --color-muted-foreground: oklch(0.68 0.014 260); /* secondary text tone */\n  --color-placeholder: oklch(0.68 0.014 260);\n\n  /* The primary action's own background — see this file's own header for what still reads the\n     accent elsewhere, unchanged. */\n  --color-primary: oklch(0.72 0.15 200);\n  --color-primary-foreground: oklch(0.14 0.02 260);\n  --color-primary-muted: oklch(0.62 0.13 200);\n\n  /* Dark surface scale: page, rail, card, active — a finer set of steps than the default\n     two-token canvas/surface pair, for a navigation rail and its active row. */\n  --color-surface-page: var(--color-canvas);\n  --color-surface-rail: oklch(0.19 0.013 260);\n  --color-surface-card: var(--color-surface);\n  --color-surface-active: oklch(0.3 0.016 260);\n\n  /* Hairline rule colour — one step, not the two-step border scale above, for a 1px divider\n     that should read as a seam rather than a bordered box. */\n  --color-hairline: oklch(0.3 0.014 260);\n\n  /* Text tones, named for what they are rather than reusing --color-foreground/-muted-foreground\n     so a consumer's own CSS can read \"text\" without knowing this is also a foreground token. */\n  --color-text: var(--color-foreground);\n  --color-text-muted: var(--color-muted-foreground);\n\n  /* Active-navigation indicator and a button's focus ring, split off --color-primary so the accent\n     stays on the primary action alone — see this file's own header. Both the same light neutral,\n     8.9:1 on every surface above, not the accent. */\n  --color-nav-active: oklch(0.86 0.02 260);\n  --color-focus-ring: oklch(0.86 0.02 260);\n}\n"
